title: v1 push — 13/15 tasks shipped, full Atelier University pack v0.1.0, foundation for live LLM↔human bridge
summary: 'Multi-agent v1 push for "locally launchable Atelier app" goal. Started with cold UX review (advisor + architect + reviewer + DX), corrected the misread that no Atelier app existed (the CLI''s atelier studio command already wraps the Studio widget in a 703-LOC inline app — the gap is creator-grade polish, not greenfield app scaffolding). 11 commits this session across 8 parallel agent tasks (orchestrated 6 paradigm:builder agents in 4 rounds + 4 pack tracks authored by me). Pack v0.1.0 shipped end-to-end — ATEL-001 (Hello Atelier) + ATEL-101 (Document Model Fundamentals) + ATEL-201 (Authoring via MCP) + ATEL-301 (Visual System), 24 entries validated. Studio v1 foundation: three load-bearing bugs fixed (autoplay-on-load, autosave silent-failure, undo state-reset), localhost security hardened (127.0.0.1 bind + Origin check via new ^localhost-only gate), welcome.atelier first-run scaffold prevents the empty-state dead-end, layer-type picker exposes Text/Shape/Image/Handle/Page-Number from the GUI, recipe overlay_rules schema landed as Phase 1.5 with translator + MCP convenience tools, atelier export-image ships single-frame PNG output, DocumentStore.onChange + AtelierStudio.applyMutation foundation for the live mutation bridge (the WS bridge wiring is the in-flight final task). Tests went 578 → 633+ (one Round 4 task still completing). Two remaining: #2 image drag-drop onto canvas (Builder G completed uncommitted; held pending Builder H), #10 WS bridge + MCP-over-WS transport (Builder H still running — the v1 close).'
