decisions:
  - id: TD-v1-app-already-exists
    decision: atelier studio CLI command is the v1 app — extend the 703-LOC inline app for v1 polish rather than scaffolding a new apps/studio package
    rationale: Cold reviewer caught that the supposed gap (no Atelier app) was wrong — the app exists; the v1 problem is creator-grade polish, not greenfield app scaffolding. Extracting inline-app to apps/studio package adds ~half-day of scaffolding cost; deferred to v1.1 once the surface is stable.
  - id: TD-overlays-as-tagged-text-layers
    decision: Handle and page-number overlays modeled as parameterized TextVisual layers with tags:[overlay], NOT as new layer types
    rationale: Architect call — keeps v1 contained, leverages existing TextVisual+TextStyle primitives, plugs into the layer-tag isolation invariant (silence-trim/caption/overlay namespaces) that already powers detected-vs-user-edited.
  - id: TD-in-memory-bridge-not-file-watch
    decision: LLM↔human mutation channel is in-memory WS bridge via DocumentStore.onChange + Studio.applyMutation, not file-watch on the .atelier file
    rationale: 'Advisor pushback against file-watch: reloading the doc on file change resets selection, undo history, scroll position — destroys the live-attribution feel. In-memory bridge preserves UI state; file save is downstream of in-memory edit.'
  - id: TD-overlay-rules-promoted-to-phase-1-5
    decision: Promote overlay_rules from reserved Phase 3 to first-class Phase 1.5; other reserved fields (caption_highlight, transition_kit, palette, audio_policy, aspect_targets) remain opaque
    rationale: v1 headline use case (carousel posts with handle + 01/05) requires overlay_rules to be real now. Other Phase 3 fields don't have current consumers so stay reserved.
  - id: TD-pack-v0-1-0-scope
    decision: Pack v0.1.0 ships ATEL-001+101+201+301; 401/501/601/701 deferred to v0.2.0
    rationale: Four-track v0.1.0 covers what a reader needs to USE Atelier today. ATEL-201 (MCP authoring) kept in v0.1.0 as the AI-native differentiator — advisor pushback against my earlier waver.
  - id: TD-testing-strategy-phased
    decision: v1 ships with vitest unit tests + welcome.atelier doc-structure snapshot. Pixel snapshot (pixelmatch) and Playwright e2e deferred to v0.2 with documented activation criteria
    rationale: Pixel snapshots need a deterministic CI runner with installed fonts; Playwright adds 30MB+ install. Both are real but not v1-blockers. Doc-structure snapshot catches schema drift, default-value changes, easing-output regressions — covers the highest-value regression class for the cost of a vitest snapshot file.
learnings:
  - 'Cold reviewer agent caught a load-bearing misread: I had assumed ''no Atelier app exists'' based on packages/studio being a widget. The reviewer inspected packages/cli/src/commands/studio.ts and found a 703-LOC inline Hono+browser app already wrapping the widget. Five of my eight ''v1 blockers'' were already built or partially built. Trust but verify on cold reads.'
  - Parallel paradigm:builder agents in background mode are highly effective when file boundaries are clean — Round 1 shipped 5 tasks in ~30 min wall clock (Builders A+B + me on pack). When file boundaries overlap (Builder G + H both touching packages/cli/src/commands/studio.ts), expect typecheck red across the in-flight period until both commit.
  - 'Builders running near their token budget often complete the work but skip the commit. Workflow: builder modifies files → tests pass → token budget exhausted before commit. Orchestrator (me) needs to inspect git status, run typecheck/test, and commit on the builder''s behalf. Use a per-builder commit-message template in the brief so this is mechanical.'
  - 'YAML quizzes with inline `{x: 0, y: 0}` or `Layer.scale.x: 2.0` syntax inside choice strings fail to parse as compact mappings. Quote them. The university validator catches the resulting ''step references entry that does not exist'' (because the unparseable quiz file isn''t indexed). Quick to diagnose once you parse the YAML directly.'
  - 'The paradigm university index caches and needs a CLI-mutating command (e.g. add note) to rebuild after a manual write — `validate` alone doesn''t trigger the rebuild. Workaround: add-then-remove a throwaway note when validating fresh hand-authored content.'
  - advisor agent is one independent reviewer, NOT 'the team' — paradigm_agent_list returns 13 active agents (architect, reviewer, dx-lens via general-purpose, etc.) which is the actual team. Multi-agent consultation requires explicit Agent dispatches in parallel, not advisor().
